<title>MEXICO: Mexico Sinaloa '97 chick pea crop seen record high.</title>
<headline>Mexico Sinaloa '97 chick pea crop seen record high.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chick pea crop in Sinaloa, Mexico's largest producing state, is estimated to reach a new record of between 90,000 and 100,000 tonnes in 1997, an industry executive said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Leobardo Angulo Batiz, the president of Grupo de Agricultores del Noroeste, told Reuters at a two-day Mexico-European Union Agribusiness Forum this year's crop follows a 1996 record chick pea, or garbanzo, harvest.</p>
<p>Grupo de Agricultores del Noroeste is a division of the Monterrey-based holding company Grupo Pulsar.</p>
<p>About 90 percent of the crop is exported, he added, with a majority, or about half, of exports sent to European markets, and the remainder mostly traded to the Middle East and South America.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
